;
; TEXTEDIT in the Multiple mode on a TEXT and an MTEXT ([0.8.1-RT11], work #939;
; card PT11, point 2; ADR 0054, point 6). Prompts from the ADR: "Current settings:
; Edit mode = Multiple", "Select an annotation object or [Undo/Mode]:", "Enter new
; text <value>:"; the MTEXT value is shown and typed with its codes on one line.
; A line is not an annotation object: no message, the prompt repeats (session of
; 2026-11-22). Objects are chosen with a typed point, as at every object request
; (ADR 0032, point 1). Each modified object is a Textedit step: U undoes the last one
; (the MTEXT) and REDO repeats it.
; ~box of "Corretto": Liberation Sans 2.1.5 advances read with fontTools (C 1479,
; o 1139, r 682, e 1139, t 569: 7398 font units), cap height 1409, ascent 1854,
; descent -434: width 7398 / 1409 * 2.5 = 13.126330731014903.
; ~lines: two paragraphs, each shorter than the width 60.
TEXT
0,0
2.5
0
Primo

MTEXT
0,-10
60,-20
riga uno
riga due

LINE
0,-30
40,-30

TEXTEDIT
20,-30
1,1
Corretto
1,-11
riga corretta\Pseconda riga

!report
U
!report
REDO
